<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45530" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Strătō^</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Străton</span></b> , ōnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Στράτων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A philosopher of Lampsacus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 1, 9, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 2,
			38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 5, 5,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A slave and physician</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Clu.
				63, 176</span></i>; <i><span class="en">64, 179</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> Stratonis turris, <i>a
				town of Palestine</i>, <i>otherwise called
				Cœsarea</i>, now <i>Kaisariyeh</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 13, 14, § 69</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
